=== morning ===
# speaker:bu_ratna
# script:morning
You are late for my stall and early for an excuse. Fortunately, I brought seeds.
* [Ask what is selling well.]
    Good produce always sells. Better produce sells before Pak Harjo finishes comparing prices.
    -> END
* [Ask for growing advice.]
    Water regularly, look at the leaves, and do not blame the seed for every mistake.
    -> END

=== day ===
# speaker:bu_ratna
# script:day
The pasaran day changes a price, not the worth of your work. Remember both numbers.
* [Ask when to sell.]
    Sell when you need room or money. Waiting for a perfect price can leave you with spoiled produce.
    -> END
* [Ask how she sets prices.]
    I look at the season, the baskets, and who has already asked me that question today.
    -> END

=== evening ===
# speaker:bu_ratna
# script:evening
Your field is quieter than the market. I like it, though I keep expecting someone to bargain with a chicken.
* [Ask if that has happened.]
    Twice. The chicken was the more reasonable customer.
    -> END
* [Offer her a place to sit.]
    Gladly. A seller spends all morning standing and all afternoon pretending her feet do not hurt.
    -> END
